## 7. Implementation

The main program is stored in `commenter.py`.

### Function definition

```python
def generate_comment(code_snippet: str) -> str:
```

The function accepts a code snippet and returns a generated comment as a string.

### Prompt construction

The prompt instructs the model to produce a concise, one-line Python comment or docstring explaining the purpose of the supplied code. The snippet is inserted dynamically into the prompt.

### API parameters

The chat completion request uses the following configuration:

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Model | `gpt-5.6-luna` |
| Message role | `user` |
| Maximum tokens | `50` |
| Temperature | `0.2` |

The API result is stored in the variable `response`. The generated text is extracted, printed to the console, and returned by `generate_comment()`.

